<Layout title="Employment conditions transparency | Royal Decree 723/2026" description="Overview of Royal Decree 723/2026 on information and transparency of employment conditions in Spain.">
<PageHero eyebrow="Legal updates · Employment" title="New rules on information and transparency of employment conditions" description="What companies and employment documents may need reviewing after Royal Decree 723/2026." primaryLabel="Review employment documents" primaryHref="/en/contact" secondaryLabel="Back to legal updates" secondaryHref="/en/legal-updates" note="Published: 15 September 2026 · Effective: 5 October 2026 · Primary source: BOE." />
<section class="section"><div class="container prose"><h2>What the regulation does</h2><p>Royal Decree 723/2026 partially transposes Directive (EU) 2019/1152 and develops the information workers must receive about essential contract terms and main working conditions. It took effect on 5 October 2026.</p><h2>Who it covers</h2><p>It applies to companies and workers covered by Article 1 of Spain’s Workers’ Statute, subject to specific rules for certain employment relationships. Its general contract-information chapter applies to relationships lasting more than four weeks; fishers and seafarers have separate chapters. Transitional rules also apply to employment relationships already in force.</p><h2>Why it matters to companies</h2><p>The practical review may involve contracts, annexes, onboarding information and internal documentation, not just one template.</p><p><a href="https://www.boe.es/eli/es/rd/2026/09/09/723/con" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read Royal Decree 723/2026 at the BOE →</a></p></div></section><CTA title="Does the new rule affect your documents?" text="We can identify which models and processes should be reviewed first." label="Contact the firm" /></Layout>
